      "Registration has traditionally required an in person visit to a district or provincial election office for biometric capture, after online pre-registration. In November 2025, reporting described a new option for National Identity Card holders to register online with biometric verification through the national ID database. Current online registration steps, deadlines, and National Identity Card linkage are To confirm against the Election Commission website, since that route was reported as newly launched in November 2025.",
      "Once on the roll, a voter does not need to re-register for the next election, subject to roll updates and corrections. Voters receive a voter identity card through the registration process. Whether the card itself must be shown at the polling station, or whether another approved identity document is accepted, is To confirm, since sources read did not settle this point."
